Weft lexicon data
=================

The files in tools/seed/ and the packs generated from them into
src/lexicon/packs/ are licensed under

    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

You may share and adapt them, including commercially, provided you give
attribution and license your adaptations under the same terms.

Why share-alike rather than the MIT licence covering the code:

  - English frequency bands derive from SUBTLEX-US by way of the wordfreq
    project. SUBTLEX is distributed under terms equivalent to CC BY-SA.
  - The ledgers in tools/seed/ (<lang>-glosses.tsv, <lang>-plurals.tsv,
    <lang>-verb-forms.tsv and the rest) cite English Wiktionary's entries and
    quote them -- a definition line, the clause of a headword line that
    prints a plural, a table's cell -- by Wiktionary contributors, under
    CC BY-SA 4.0. Each line names the entry it quotes as
    wikt:<language>:<title>, which is the section for that language of the
    page https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/<title>, an underscore standing for
    a space.
  - Where coverage is extended from Wiktionary via wiktextract / kaikki.org,
    that data is CC BY-SA and GFDL.

Latin glosses and genders are checked against Lewis & Short, A Latin
Dictionary (1879), and glosses against Whitaker's Words, both public domain.
Old English glosses are checked against Bosworth-Toller, An Anglo-Saxon
Dictionary (1898) and Clark Hall, A Concise Anglo-Saxon Dictionary (1894),
both public domain. Public-domain sources impose no conditions; they are
listed for scholarly honesty rather than for compliance. Etymology claims
cite the Online Etymology Dictionary (Douglas Harper,
https://www.etymonline.com), which is not openly licensed, and is credited
in every pack whose ledgers cite it.

Attribution is carried inside every generated pack, in meta.attribution, so it
travels with the data rather than living only in this file. Each pack names
the sources its own claims were read in, and tests/tools/attribution.test.ts
fails on a pack that does not name a source its ledgers cite, or that names
one they never cite.
